# A Windows path gets the path help even when one of its escapes (`\n`) happens to be valid.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'C:\data\new.csv' | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..32
  PIPELINE@0..31
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..22
      STRING@5..22 "'C:\\data\\new.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
    PIPE@23..24 "|"
    WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
    TAKE_OP@25..31
      IDENT@25..29 "take"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      LITERAL@30..31
        LONG@30..31 "1"
  WHITESPACE@31..32 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\d`
  --> query:1:9
  |
1 | from 'C:\data\new.csv' | take 1
  |         ^^ not a valid escape
  |
  = help: if this is a Windows path, use a verbatim string `@'C:\data\new.csv'` or forward slashes `'C:/data/new.csv'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`
